Third-party components included in lmdraw distributions

Project code
------------
The lmdraw source and the vendored lmcode-cpp header are licensed under MIT;
see LICENSE.

LunaSVG 3.5.0 and PlutoVG 1.3.1
--------------------------------
The statically linked vector parser and rasterizer source is vendored in
third_party/lunasvg at upstream commit 83c58df8103dc7dca423dfd824992af94d49bed6.
LunaSVG and its bundled PlutoVG carry MIT licenses. PlutoVG includes raster
routines derived from the FreeType project under its FreeType Project License
(FTL), and the stb image and TrueType helpers carry public-domain notices.
Full MIT and FTL texts are in licenses/; the source files retain their original
stb notices.

Noto Sans and Noto Sans Math
----------------------------
Noto Sans Regular, Noto Sans Bold, and Noto Sans Math Regular TrueType fonts
are compiled into the executable and are licensed under SIL Open Font License
1.1. The font copyright notice and full license are in assets/fonts/OFL.txt
and licenses/Noto-OFL-1.1.txt.

Linux C and C++ runtimes
------------------------
Linux release binaries link the system glibc dynamically (LGPL-2.1-or-later;
glibc >= 2.35 required) and statically include libstdc++ and libgcc runtime
objects, which are GPL-3.0-or-later with GCC Runtime Library Exception 3.1.
Copies of the relevant license texts are in licenses/.

Platform system libraries
-------------------------
macOS binaries link the operating-system libraries supplied by macOS. Windows
binaries use the MinGW-w64 toolchain with static compiler runtimes and import
only platform system libraries.
